From 1ccfa28aab01071545bc7345a3e99a2ebedfac40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ricardo Pardini <ricardo@pardini.net>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 17:27:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] DEBUG: tcpm/fusb302: USB-PD bring-up tracing for Blade 3

- print all tcpm/fusb302 dev_*() to console, prefixed with ms since
  power-on and the parent I2C bus (both FUSB302s are usb-typec@22)
- log auto-probe decision with connector label, own/partner PDOs, init
  state, PD TX status, hard resets sent/received, polling summary
- fusb302: dump registers before sw reset, after init and before low
  power; decode PD messages left in the RX FIFO by a previous session
- TYPEC_TCPM_DEBUG_VERBOSE (default off): register write trace and full
  PD message/PDO dumps; slow enough to miss tSenderResponse
- rockchip SPL: timestamp console-up and jump to next stage
- rock5b board: print CRU GLB_RST_ST (0 = power-on reset)
- tcpm: add missing newline to "probing Type-C port manager..."

Armbian only, not for upstream.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Ricardo Pardini <ricardo@pardini.net>
---
 arch/arm/mach-rockchip/spl.c              |   5 +
 board/radxa/rock5b-rk3588/rock5b-rk3588.c |  15 ++-
 drivers/usb/tcpm/Kconfig                  |   9 ++
 drivers/usb/tcpm/fusb302.c                | 131 +++++++++++++++++++++-
 drivers/usb/tcpm/tcpm-debug.h             |  91 +++++++++++++++
 drivers/usb/tcpm/tcpm-uclass.c            |  22 +++-
 drivers/usb/tcpm/tcpm.c                   |  57 +++++++++-
 7 files changed, 316 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 drivers/usb/tcpm/tcpm-debug.h

